# Copy to ~/.vinegar/watchdog.env and `chmod 600` it. Both values are secrets
# in the sense that matters: anyone holding them can silence your alerting or
# page you at will. Leave either blank and that channel is skipped, which is
# how you run the watchdog with only one of them.

# A healthchecks.io check. Set its period to 5 minutes and its grace to 15, to
# match the plist's StartInterval. This is the one that reports the machine
# being off, because it alerts on the pings stopping rather than on anything
# the machine manages to send.
HEALTHCHECK_URL=""

# An ntfy.sh topic. Any unguessable string; it exists as soon as you publish to
# it. This is the fast path for a crash the watchdog is still alive to see.
# Subscribe to it in the ntfy app, and point your healthchecks.io alert at it
# too so both channels land in the same place.
NTFY_TOPIC=""
